==Battleground==
*20 [[Diabrollow]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Two Can]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[R.Ost]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
**2 [[Diabrollow]]s spawn, delay 1.33~2.67 seconds<sup>40f~80f</sup>.
**10 [[Diabrollow]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**1 [[Two Can]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Say hell(o) to Diabrollow, whose Knockback ability combined with [[Mini-Wave]] means that you'll quickly go crazy after a few stages with it. As a [[Brollow]] variant, simply use a hard-hitting unit to remove as many chances for it to rebound as possible.

For this stage in general, use your usual methods of dealing with R.Ost and Two Can.
[[Hitman Cat]] is an excellent choice as a damage dealer for R.Ost, while [[Pizza Cat]] proves very useful here to blow up Two Can. [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rushers]] like [[Fishman Cat]] and [[Bullet Train Cat]] will also work here.

Talented Li'l Mohawk Cat, when combined with the [[Mini-Saurus (Combo)|Mini-Saurus]] Catcombo can be a great tertiary meatshield, being immune to waves and holding some ground if Two Can nukes your meatshields or Diabrollow knocks everything back.

